{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"929377169382ef94fc9269f7b427e160a7f1389beabc8063e166afe4fd74a0d3","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-bot LLM service / Bedrock integration","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py::build_bedrock_provider","REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION","AWS_DEFAULT_REGION","BedrockProvider","boto3.session.Session().region_name","pydantic_ai.exceptions.UserError","LLMConfigError","tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py","infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md"],"problem_keywords":["bedrock","region resolution","llm provider","cutover failure","configuration"],"propositions":["review-bot container lacks AWS region configuration (REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION and AWS_DEFAULT_REGION unset), causing boto3.client('bedrock-runtime') to raise NoRegionError at provider construction","pydantic-ai-slim catches botocore NoRegionError and re-raises UserError (not a subclass of rebar LLMError), so existing fail-closed exception handlers do not catch it","boto3 region resolution respects AWS_DEFAULT_REGION but not AWS_REGION alone on botocore 1.43.58, and IMDS reachability supplies credentials but never region","Bedrock cutover hard-fails at LLM-Review gate because story eb6e has no cross-provider fallback when region is unconfigured","CloudWatch voter metrics silently no-op due to the same missing-region root cause, breaking eb6e's rollback alarm plan"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787903661969406001,"uuid":"bbdd6430-155b-486b-bc54-090e6ead64ce"}